    <string-array name="faq_answers">
        <item>Mi Remote can control most appliances that use IR remotes, such as TVs, air conditioners, and set-top boxes. Devices that do not use IR remote control, such as toy cars or some Bluetooth or wireless lights, are not supported.</item>
        <item>"Phones with an IR blaster can use Mi Remote's IR features. Most other phones can only use WLAN remote control. Supported IR phones include Xiaomi 6, Xiaomi 5, Xiaomi 5s Plus, Xiaomi 5X, Xiaomi 5c, Xiaomi 4/4C/4S, Xiaomi Note 3, Xiaomi Note 2, Mi Max 2, Mi Max, Redmi Note 5/4/2/3, Redmi 5/5 Plus/5A/5X/4/4A/4X/3, Samsung Galaxy S3/S4/S5/S6, Note 2/3/4, Huawei Honor 6, Honor 6 Plus, Honor 7, and HTC One series."</item>
        <item>The number of brands shown depends on your network speed. If the network is normal, all device brands are loaded online. If the network is slow, the app switches to the built-in compact IR database, so fewer brands are shown. If you still want to see all brands, enable “Use online data for new remotes” in Settings. Loading the brand list may take some time because of network conditions.</item>
        <item>The remote data you matched is not for this air conditioner. The second matching button turns off the air conditioner. Follow the prompts on your phone and select “Responds” only when the air conditioner actually turns off, then match it again.</item>
        <item>First check whether the TV remote is an IR remote. If it is not, Mi Remote cannot control it by IR. If it is an IR remote, select the correct brand in Mi Remote and tap each test button several times to confirm whether the TV responds. When testing the power button, wait a little longer because some TVs take more time to power on.</item>
        <item>Binding a set-top box means adding the remote for the set-top box you are using. After it is added, you can view the channel guide and schedule on the TV Programs page. If a program is currently playing, you can tap “Change channel” from the program details to switch to that channel. Set-top boxes include two main types: traditional set-top boxes and IPTV set-top boxes.</item>
        <item>You do not need to sign in to control home appliances or view TV programs. However, we recommend signing in with a Xiaomi account.</item>
        <item>Your phone does not support IR transmission. It can control Xiaomi Box, Xiaomi TV, and some standard Android smart boxes/TVs over WLAN. If your TV/box and phone are connected to the same WLAN but still cannot be found, check your router settings and make sure AP isolation is turned off.</item>
        <item>Xiaomi split TVs, TV hosts, Mi Box 3 Enhanced Edition, and Mi Box mini do not support IR remote control. They support WLAN control and Bluetooth control. Connect your phone to the same WLAN as the TV. After the TV is powered on, Mi Remote can automatically find the Xiaomi TV.</item>
        <item>Most lights currently use radio-frequency remote control instead of IR remote control, so Mi Remote does not support them.</item>
        <item>This error appears if microphone permission is not enabled for Mi Remote. Go to System settings > Permission management > App permissions > Mi Remote, find the microphone permission, and allow it to use voice remote normally.</item>
    </string-array>
